{"id": "1d77b7e4a18643e5f8840f8d78a760aa182e6cbd", "document_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf", "text": "The gearbox transmission lubrication in service was 2640 semi-synthetic, 15W/40 viscosity. All signals were record at speed 45 RPS and 15 RPS. System Description Vessel and Transmission: INS Haifa emp", "section_title": "Executive Summary", "page_start": 1, "page_end": 1, "type": "text", "anchor": "p1-t2", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": [], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [15, 45], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf#p1:Summary/p1-t2", "section_raw": "Summary", "file_title": "Gear wear Failure.pdf"}}
{"id": "ab6e07c4a3339fd0bad1ee902e4a4f5dd03ffba8", "document_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf", "text": "The lubrication system features dual pumps and automated thermal bypass valves, ensuring continuous and reliable delivery of lubricant to the sliding bearing housing. • Mechanical Mounting and Bearing", "section_title": "Failure Progression", "page_start": 1, "page_end": 1, "type": "text", "anchor": "p1-t2", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": [], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf#p1:Timeline/p1-t2", "section_raw": "Timeline", "file_title": "Sliding_Bearing_Failure_Investigation_Report.pdf"}}
{"id": "ab01edb280ea0a799dc9ccfffac1a6c2fe18cf6f", "document_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf", "text": "2 | P a g e\n\nImaging: Following each measurement day, tooth-flank photographs were taken from the driven gear, using a camera integrated with the inspection microscope available in the lab (images arc detected. Shaft alignment was visually assessed for signs of deformation, and both the shaft supports and thrust bearings were confirmed to be securely mounted. The shaft was manually rotated and show - No abnormal gear contact, or unbalance speed (speed fluctuations). In Spectral Domain Analysis, the companion spectrograms and FFT snapshots captured during operation showed a narrow-band signature • Temperature monitoring: Inlet and outlet temperatures were recorded at 48.5°C and 57.8°C, respectively, with a manually calculated differential of approximately 9.3°C, remaining within the expected", "section_title": "Results and Analysis", "page_start": 2, "page_end": 2, "type": "text", "anchor": "p2-t1", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": ["accelerometer", "camera"], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf#p2:Analysis/p2-t1", "section_raw": "Analysis", "file_title": "Gear wear Failure.pdf"}}
{"id": "1867476273db623fc646a7d3ef9a2157d5d5edd9", "document_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf", "text": "3 | P a g e\n\nimages from February 13, subtle modifications of the tooth profile were visible: part of the contact area had been removed, showing the first physical evidence of surface alteration. This", "section_title": "Failure Progression", "page_start": 3, "page_end": 3, "type": "text", "anchor": "p3-t1", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": ["camera"], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf#p3:Timeline/p3-t1", "section_raw": "Timeline", "file_title": "Gear wear Failure.pdf"}}
{"id": "92884dabb356c86a29815a2804c8caa4e2798762", "document_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf", "text": "previous five days of logged vibration data, the technician found no comparable upward trend. Emergence of Anomalies (07:10–07:30) At 07:15, the on-duty technician reported a mild knocking sound origi", "section_title": "Results and Analysis", "page_start": 3, "page_end": 3, "type": "text", "anchor": "p3-t1", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": ["accelerometer"], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf#p3:Analysis/p3-t1", "section_raw": "Analysis", "file_title": "Sliding_Bearing_Failure_Investigation_Report.pdf"}}
{"id": "84d889c9f3f7c71efdf4b5477f3f4030a911492d", "document_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf", "text": "Crucially, the timeline of evidence shows that the photographs provided the first definitive indications of wear, while the vibration data only followed with measurable confirmation by April 23. This", "section_title": "Failure Progression", "page_start": 3, "page_end": 3, "type": "text", "anchor": "p3-t2", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": ["accelerometer", "camera"], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf#p3:Timeline/p3-t2", "section_raw": "Timeline", "file_title": "Gear wear Failure.pdf"}}
{"id": "3ecce0547aee936bacab6db4a56da30653e30a95", "document_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf", "text": "• Lubrication System Rerouting: The lubrication system was switched to the secondary circulation loop to isolate the primary filter, which was suspected of partial blockage or contamination. • Auxilia", "section_title": "Results and Analysis", "page_start": 3, "page_end": 3, "type": "text", "anchor": "p3-t2", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": [], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf#p3:Analysis/p3-t2", "section_raw": "Analysis", "file_title": "Sliding_Bearing_Failure_Investigation_Report.pdf"}}
{"id": "7902c403e65c688e595f85dd4416400d9ad3d240", "document_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf", "text": "4 | P a g e\n\nbroadband noise floor above the mesh harmonics also rose noticeably compared to the baseline, confirming a spread of high-frequency energy consistent with contact roughening. At 15 RPS, a", "section_title": "Baseline Condition", "page_start": 4, "page_end": 4, "type": "text", "anchor": "p4-t1", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": [], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [15], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "gear-wear-failure.pdf#p4:Text/p4-t1", "section_raw": "Text", "file_title": "Gear wear Failure.pdf"}}
{"id": "69890a69da17856cc57a371e929c80303029f01d", "document_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf", "text": "exceeded 80°C, and the audible knocking from the bearing housing intensified in both volume and frequency. Controlled Return to Port (07:50–10:15) At 07:50, following confirmation of mechanical degrad - Spectral content displaying organized sideband families and a rising broadband floor across successive days. This stage thus marks the progression from micro-texture alteration into geometrically s A comprehensive metallurgical investigation included: • SEM (scanning electron microscopy) showing micro-crack formation and fatigue bands. • EDS (energy-dispersive spectroscopy) confirming elevated i", "section_title": "Results and Analysis", "page_start": 4, "page_end": 4, "type": "text", "anchor": "p4-t1", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": ["accelerometer"], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf#p4:Analysis/p4-t1", "section_raw": "Analysis", "file_title": "Sliding_Bearing_Failure_Investigation_Report.pdf"}}
{"id": "1d1e53b95029ba843c565a355b0f1d042faecd9a", "document_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf", "text": "The root cause was determined to be a loss of hydrodynamic film due to eccentric shaft loading. Secondary contributors included one mounting bolt discovered post-failure to have <60% of required prelo Contact regions had lost most of their original geometry, and scarring extended across the majority of the flank surface. Vibration measurements reinforced this terminal state: spectra were dominated By 16:30, the lubrication system was flushed with solvent and replenished with fresh ISO VG 220 oil. Concurrently, seawater cooling circuits were re-pressurized, and all temperature and pressure senso", "section_title": "Results and Analysis", "page_start": 5, "page_end": 5, "type": "text", "anchor": "p5-t1", "source_id": null, "date": null, "date_start": null, "date_end": null, "wear_stage": null, "sensor_type": ["accelerometer"], "measurement_type": [], "speed": [], "extras": {"entities": ["INS Haifa", "MG-5025A"], "source_chunk_id": "sliding_bearing_failure_investigation_report.pdf#p5:Analysis/p5-t1", "section_raw": "Analysis", "file_title": "Sliding_Bearing_Failure_Investigation_Report.pdf"}}
